o maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m Substituting \(z = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\) into the expression, we get:[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) = 4(75 \cos \theta + 117 \sin \theta + i(75 \sin \theta - 117 \cos \theta))[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4} \cdot \frac{\cos \theta - i \sin \theta}{\cos^2 \theta + \sin^2 \theta} = (24 - 36i)(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta) = 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta - i(24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta + 117 \sin \theta + i(75 \sin \theta - 117 \cos \theta)) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta - i(24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m = 4(75 \cos \theta + 117 \sin \theta) + 24 \cos \theta + i(4(75 \sin \theta - 117 \cos \theta) - (24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta))[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m = (300 \cos \theta + 468 \sin \theta + 24 \cos \theta) + i(300 \sin \theta - 468 \cos \theta - 24 \sin \theta + 36 \cos \theta)[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m = (324 \cos \theta + 468 \sin \theta) + i(276 \sin \theta - 432 \cos \theta)[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta + 468 \sin \theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 468\), so the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta + 468 \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 468^2}\):[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 219024} = \sqrt{324000} = 570[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(\boxed{570}\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [ground_truth] 540[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [score] -1.0[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [acc] False[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [pred] dapo:570,qwen:qwen_evaluated[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [dapo_result] {'score': -1.0, 'acc': False, 'pred': '570'}[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [qwen_result] {'score': 0.0, 'acc': False, 'pred': 'qwen_evaluated'}[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [dapo_correct] False[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [qwen_correct] False[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['reward']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['score']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['acc']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['pred']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['dapo_result']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['qwen_result']: 960[36m(TaskRun