ta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta).[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m The real part of the expression is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta = 324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta.[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m To maximize \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\), we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -468\), so the maximum value is:[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \[[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 219024} = \sqrt{324000} = 570.[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m \][36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(\boxed{570}\).[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [ground_truth] 540[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [score] -1.0[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [acc] False[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [pred] dapo:570,qwen:qwen_evaluated[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [dapo_result] {'score': -1.0, 'acc': False, 'pred': '570'}[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [qwen_result] {'score': 0.0, 'acc': False, 'pred': 'qwen_evaluated'}[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [dapo_correct] False[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m [qwen_correct] False[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['reward']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['score']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['acc']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['pred']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['dapo_result']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len reward_extra_infos_dict['qwen_result']: 960[36m(TaskRunner pid=2945368)[0m len 